.TH XD\-EVENTVWR 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-eventvwr \- Event Viewer for the systemd journal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-eventvwr
.RB [ application | security | system ]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xd\-eventvwr
is Windows XP's Event Viewer, reading the systemd journal.
XP's three logs are views of it:
.TP
.B Application
The user's own programs and user services.
.TP
.B Security
Authentication: the auth facilities, sudo, polkit, sshd...
.TP
.B System
The kernel and the system's services.
.PP
It only reads.
Without membership of the
.B systemd\-journal
(or
.B wheel
or
.BR adm )
group, only the user's own journal can be read; the window says so.
.PP
The argument opens that log (in any case).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR xd\-admintools (1)
